# Data files are checksummed in src/ssapy_data/manifest.json, so their bytes
# must be identical on every platform. Without this, git applies its text
# heuristic to the ASCII-ish files here (the .egm gravity-model headers in
# particular) and rewrites line endings per checkout: Windows gets CRLF, Linux
# CI gets LF, the same committed file hashes differently, and
# scripts/update_manifest.py emits a different manifest depending where it ran.
#
# Concretely: egm84.egm was 822 bytes on Windows and 800 on Linux, egm96.egm
# 776 vs 753, wgs84.egm 745 vs 724 -- one byte per header line. CI's manifest
# check failed for exactly that reason.
src/ssapy_data/data/** -text
